gosh seam 22: The cipher's key may be made from its 16 octets (Base64Key::of_octets), an addition to its ABI.

For:   REQ22/SHAPE-1 (since v22, the seam may add to a core domain's ABI where a part of gosh needs
       it). gosh's meetup holds a ticket's key as 16 bytes; the cipher took a key only as 22
       letters of base64, so gosh wrote the bytes as base64 with the cipher's own inside
       (imp/base64.h), for the key to read them back, and seam/DOMAINS allowed that reach. The
       allow goes.
What:  An addition, and nothing else changed: Base64Key::of_octets( octets ) is the key of those
       16 octets as they are, and throws CryptoException ("Key must represent 16 octets.", as
       the constructor from text says) if there are not 16. A private constructor makes the
       key's storage, zeroed, for it. No byte of the protocol changes, and nothing that was
       there behaves otherwise.
Where: src/crypto/crypto.h (Base64Key); src/crypto/imp/crypto.cc.
Kind:  one static function and one private constructor added to the cipher's ABI.
From:  the core at the pin: src/crypto/crypto.h, src/crypto/crypto.cc (moved under imp/ by patch 12).
Pin:   upstream mosh at decd9b705eb81626f694335b8d5940538beb06da; cut against the result of the patch before it.

